imagine a planet of endless sand and  scorching sun  a world where every day is a race for  survival and every night a fearsome  competition for resources the infamous  desert planet of tatooine located in a  galaxy far far away is known for being  an inhospitable wasteland yet the  creatures that brave this unforgiving  environment are truly fascinating and  possess hidden intricacies that deserve  to be studied further  so for this entry into the archive i'll  be documenting this arid biosphere first  hand analyzing the biology of these  extreme life forms and seeing how their  survival strategies compare to those  present in earth's deserts so join me in  a landspeeder on this voyage across the  desert as we uncover the mysteries of  tatooine  the planet of tatooine orbits a rare  binary star system meaning it has two  suns with the smaller sun in a stable  orbit around the larger one  on the surface of tatooine one can  certainly feel the heat of both suns at  all times as can the animals that live  here beginning our journey on the vast  expanse known as the dune sea life in  this region is highly specialized to  survive the merciless heat  peering through my macro binoculars i  spot a group of woolly banthas these  hearty megafauna are the preferred  method of transportation for the local  tuscan populace in a staple of tatooine  wildlife a large furry animal might seem  poorly suited for a hot desert  environment but we can find a desert  life form with a similar strategy in the  earth camel  camels are experts at keeping cool in  part through specialized shaggy fur that  helps keep their body temperatures low  to prevent excess moisture loss so it's  likely the banthas can enter the deserts  of tatooine thanks to similar  adaptations  but beating the heat is one thing to  survive on tatooine the banthas must  also find food and water to discover the  bantha's food source one must dig  underground this is a black melon a  cactus-like species which like many  forms of cacti is a precious source of  water in this arid ecosystem  once again earth camels supplement their  bulk with a similar food source grazing  on cacti whenever they get the chance  while you or i might struggle to stomach  plants like this it's no trouble for  desert specialists like the camel or the  bantha  so while the dune sea seems barren the  surprisingly dense network of  underground vegetation means large  creatures such as the bantha don't go  hungry  if they know where to look  but it's not just the banthas who drink  of the black melon the tuscan clans a  group of mysterious sapient lifeforms  that call this unforgiving desert their  home also know all the ins and outs of  the dune sea i initially hoped to  document some of their knowledge but  tuscans are highly distrustful of  off-worlders  they weren't interested in conversing  without their masks or even with them so  my questions about this planet's ecology  go unanswered for now  feeling my welcome is well past worn out  it's time i set off on my landspeeder  once more and document the next life  form of tatooine  heading through a nero canyon i spot a  fearsome massive and unfortunately for  me these mid-sized reptilian predators  move in packs coordinating in intricate  groups to take down their prey  the massive pack structure is similar to  those of spotted hyenas on earth with  both species living in large factions  that coordinate to apprehend animals far  larger than themselves and sharing in  the spoils once the hunt is over  fortunately for me this pack  surprisingly isn't wild but are the  domesticated allies of the same tuscan  clan i spoke to before as it turns out  domesticated massive serve as loyal  guard dogs across tuscan societies  deciding to spend another night with the  clan i learn more about the massives  like how their dorsal spines aren't just  for defense but also show the creature's  age through their length and although  i'm still a little worried the massives  haven't stopped thinking about eating me  i'm excited to find the tuscans are  opening up to my questions  a tuscan storyteller i interview informs  me that their people believe that  thousands of years ago tatooine was  covered in rainforest and the dune sea  itself was an ocean of flowing water  such an extreme transformation might  seem unlikely but shells and other  fossils found in the dune sea on a prior  expedition corroborate this theory the  process by which fertile land becomes  desert is called desertification  and it seems this process began on  tatooine around 25 000 years ago  some claim the desertification of  tatooine was brought on by off-world or  activity while others theorize it was a  natural process caused by the planet's  twin suns in any case it's something  i'll have to keep in mind as i consider  the lineage of the species that live  here  the next morning a commotion stirs  through the camp a trap has caught a  nocturnal wart twisting out the  toad-like creature careens across the  sand typically warts are most active at  night where they feed on rodents like  womp rats and anything else they can  ambush with their shockingly long  tongues  these tongues resemble those of earth  chameleons which can also lash out with  amazing speed at unsuspecting prey like  the wart the chameleon's tongue is  stretchable to almost twice the animal's  length and is powered by spirally wound  protein fibers which can store energy  like a stretched rubber band  yet soon this predator will become prey  one quick blaster bolt  and it's all over this wart will help  feed the clan and their massives a  little longer to survive on tatooine one  must take what one can get  setting off towards the western reaches  a spot in the distance an intimidating  creature rising up from the sand  this six-limbed feral beast is a  tatooine sand date its target is a wild  massif which the giant sand ape makes  short work of  this is not a creature one should mess  with while their name and muscular  anatomy mirrors large primates like  gorillas the sand apes ambush hunting  strategy is actually much closer to a  very different kind of life form  in the sahara desert a slightly smaller  predator swims under the sand the sand  fish is a type of reptile that buries  itself within the dunes then when prey  gets close enough it surfaces and  snatches it up just like the sand ape of  tatooine and now that the sand ape has  subdued the massif it's time to head in  the other direction before it makes me  its next meal  cresting over a sand dune i spot a herd  of lethargic dewbacks these  thick-skinned reptiles are frequently  used as mounts both by travelers and  those of a more sinister nature their  name however comes from their seldom  glimpsed habit of licking the morning  dew from their backs to stay hydrated a  desert animal drinking collected dew  might sound miraculous but namab desert  beetles which i've discussed on this  channel before actually have a  convergent survival strategy on misty  desert mornings they stand on their  heads and let the dew that collects on  their backs drip down into their mouths  and with fog in the air today these  dewbacks likely have the same idea on a  world with twin suns all water is  precious  but there are far more dangerous  creatures under the twin suns i've yet  to document rancors are massive  predators prized in the underground  market for their fighting capabilities  paying to study one specimen i've found  they live up to their fearsome  reputation with their long arms they  seem somewhat unsteady on two feet with  a posture reminiscent of the fighting  stance of a territorial grizzly bear  with their long claws and powerful brawn  grizzlies are perhaps the closest thing  on earth to a rancor  on their hind legs these bears can tower  over seven feet or two meters tall but  as imposing as grizzlies are a  full-grown rancor can easily reach 16  feet or 5 meters tall which puts into  perspective just how dangerous these  gigantic hulks of muscle really are and  since rancors are not native to tatooine  their introduction has wreaked havoc on  the local ecosystem  but much like grizzly bears there's  another side to the seemingly vicious  rancor  my studies suggest young rancors  actually imprint on whatever species  they first interact with during an early  period of development  imprinting isn't unheard of in earth's  animal kingdom and is present in young  birds especially but it might be a  little surprising to see such a behavior  in a beast as brutal as a rancor like  most creatures rancors are much more  complicated than they first appear  that being said there is one life form  in particular that i've been  apprehensive to study up close  in the pit of carcoon dwells the  carnivorous sarlacc appearing as a giant  mouth buried in the sand local testimony  indicates that under the surface the  sarlacc's body is over 300 feet or 100  meters long  a diagram from the field guide of the  interplanetary naturalist terrell  whitlatch gives us a more complete look  at the sarlacc's body underneath the  sand this diagram shows us that feeding  tentacles extend from the creature's  posterior end drawing in nutrients from  the surrounding sand like the roots of a  plant indeed the ever-confounding  sarlacc may be more plant than animal  but the sarlacc still feeds on live prey  that falls into its fanged mouth  while an organism relying on prey to  fall directly into its domain might  sound strange one species on earth does  something quite similar this pit belongs  to an ant lion an insect eating predator  that digs steep holes in the sand that  almost look like miniature sarlacc pits  the antlion waits at the bottom of the  trap for an ant to tumble down the slope  which the ant lion then slowly devours  curiously there are similar rumors that  the sarlacc also digests its food over a  long period of time but the only way to  determine whether or not this is true is  to get a closer look  so i'm lowering a flashlight equipped  camera inside the creature's gullet this  is a nerve-wracking operation as the  beast might awaken and attack the light  at any moment navigating the camera down  a stomach cavity i find it's difficult  to see anything turning on the  high-powered beam we've found the  half-digested remains of an unlucky  former meal while gross this discovery  seems to confirm the theory of the  sarlacc slow digestive system  unfortunately it seems the sarlacc has  had enough of our prodding and turns  aggressive time to quickly pull the  camera back up to the surface and leave  this place forever  on tatooine one might assume the sarlacc  would be the top predator but there is a  single final life form on this planet  large enough to eat sarlacc while  refueling at a town i notice the sand  begins to vibrate when the ground shakes  like this  every life form from the tiny scurriers  to the largest banthas know it means  trouble one older bantha isn't quick  enough from the ground bursts an  enormous predator which vanishes just as  quickly with its meal that was a crate  dragon the most elusive and deadly  creature on tatooine  the bones of juvenile crate dragons can  sometimes be glimpsed upon the dunes but  when great dragons reach their adult  form they're virtually invincible this  will be a very challenging species to  study indeed  reuniting with the tuscan clan from  earlier i agree to travel with them to  the site of a crate dragon cave the  tuscans make a pilgrimage here regularly  as they've studied its digestive cycle  for generations and feed the beast  banthas to keep it satiated  from the depths of the cave the creature  emerges  this time the dragon seems satisfied  with its meal and retreats back under  the sand  for now  according to the tuscans the krait  dragons have another terrifying habit  when they feel threatened projecting  corrosive venom directly from their  mouths which causes their target to  dissolve  while spitting venom might seem unusual  there are several species of spitting  cobras that have a similar defense when  threatened these snakes can contract  muscles around their venom glands and  launch venom from their needle-like  fangs  and like the krait dragon some spitting  cobras can launch their deadly venom  more than three times the length of  their bodies crate dragon venom however  isn't true venom but an acidic fluid  that helps them digest their food  we're fortunate that the crate dragon  wasn't in a spitting mood today  yet one way or another eventually  everything on tatooine meets its end to  the south an adult crate dragon has died  and other species benefit from the  resources its body leaves behind  the clan i'm traveling with is  particularly effective at breaking down  the different parts of these leviathans  after they expire but there is one body  part in particular they seem to be  searching for a young hunter has found a  rare krait dragon pearl these pearls are  formed the same way as the pearls of  earth mollusks the process begins when a  small irritant like a grain of sand  finds its way inside the life form a  crystallized substance known as [ __ ]  then forms around the irritant and over  time the layers build up and form a  pearl  but it's an uncommon occurrence in krait  dragons and hence finding this valuable  pearl is a tremendous triumph for the  clan  it's been an incredible trek across  tatooine while all life forms here have  to endure the same conditions no two  life forms have adapted to this planet's  unique challenges in the same way we've  learned much about these survival  strategies on our expedition but with  the twin suns high in the afternoon sky  the time has come at last to say goodbye  to this unexpectedly teeming planet  as always thanks for watching if you  enjoyed this entry please lend your  support to help make videos like this  possible by liking subscribing and  hitting the notification icon to stay up  to date on all things curious  see you in the next video  you
 

